A clause that carries the `=` but names no field before it has nothing to match on, so it is
rejected exactly like a clause with no `=` at all rather than filtering on an empty key.

-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where '=done'
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: malformed --where clause (expected k=v, k!=v, k:in=a,b, k:gt=n or k:lt=n): =done
